    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-day owner creation limit in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler backing `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added a guard in `addOwner` (right after the candidate's `registrationDate` defaults to today) that returns `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` when the daily limit is reached:\n```java\nif (isDailyLimitReached()) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n}\n```\n\n2. Added a helper matching the style of the existing quota checks (e.g. `isCityAtCapacity`):\n```java\nprivate boolean isDailyLimitReached() {\n    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();\n    long count = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n        .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))\n        .count();\n    return count >= 100;\n}\n```\n\nIt counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the current date and rejects once that reaches 100, so the 101st create today gets a 429. The acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` and the full suite pass.",
